    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L12-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "12.3: Multiplication on the Complex Plane",
      "SourceExcerpt": "If \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are positive numbers, is it true that \\(\\sqrt{ab}=\\sqrt{a}\\sqrt{b}\\)? Explain how you know.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l12.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L12-ACTIVITY-020",
      "SourceSection": "12.3: Multiplication on the Complex Plane",
      "SourceExcerpt": "If \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are negative numbers, is it true that \\(\\sqrt{ab}=\\sqrt{a}\\sqrt{b}\\)? Explain how you know.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l12.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L12-ACTIVITY-021",
      "SourceSection": "12.3: Multiplication on the Complex Plane",
      "SourceExcerpt": "When we add a real number with an imaginary number, we get a complex number. We usually write complex numbers as:",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l12.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L12-ACTIVITY-022",
      "SourceSection": "12.3: Multiplication on the Complex Plane",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle a + bi\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l12.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L12-ACTIVITY-023",
      "SourceSection": "12.3: Multiplication on the Complex Plane",
      "SourceExcerpt": "where \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are real numbers. We say that \\(a\\) is the real part and \\(bi\\) is the imaginary part.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l12.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L12-ACTIVITY-024",
      "SourceSection": "12.3: Multiplication on the Complex Plane",
      "SourceExcerpt": "To add (or subtract) two complex numbers, we add (or subtract) the real parts and add (or subtract) the imaginary parts. For example:",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l12.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L12-ACTIVITY-025",
      "SourceSection": "12.3: Multiplication on the Complex Plane",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle (2 + 3i )+(4 + 5i) = (2 + 4) + (3i + 5i) = 6 + 8i\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l12.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L12-ACTIVITY-026",
      "SourceSection": "12.3: Multiplication on the Complex Plane",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle (2 + 3i )-(4 + 5i) = (2 - 4) + (3i - 5i) = \\text-2 - 2i\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l12.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L12-ACTIVITY-027",
      "SourceSection": "12.3: Multiplication on the Complex Plane",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle (a+bi) + (c+di) = (a+c) + (b+d)i\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l12.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L12-ACTIVITY-028",
      "SourceSection": "12.3: Multiplication on the Complex Plane",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle (a+bi) - (c+di) = (a-c) + (b - d)i\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l12.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L12-ACTIVITY-029",
      "SourceSection": "12.3: Multiplication on the Complex Plane",
      "SourceExcerpt": "When we raise an imaginary number to a power, we can use the fact that \\(i^2=\\text-1\\) to write the result in the form \\(a+bi\\). For example, \\((4i)^3=4i \\boldcdot 4i \\boldcdot 4i\\). We can group the \\(i\\) factors together to see how to…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l12.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L12-ACTIVITY-030",
      "SourceSection": "12.3: Multiplication on the Complex Plane",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\begin{align*} 4i \\boldcdot 4i \\boldcdot 4i &= (4 \\boldcdot 4 \\boldcdot 4) \\boldcdot (i \\boldcdot i \\boldcdot i) \\\\ &= 64 \\boldcdot (i^2 \\boldcdot i) \\\\ &= 64 \\boldcdot \\text-1 \\boldcdot i \\\\ &= \\text-64i \\end{align*} \\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l12.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L12-ACTIVITY-031",
      "SourceSection": "12.3: Multiplication on the Complex Plane",
      "SourceExcerpt": "So in this example, \\(a\\) is 0 and \\(b\\) is -64.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l12.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L12-ACTIVITY-032",
      "SourceSection": "12.3: Multiplication on the Complex Plane",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A number in the complex plane. It can be written as \\(a + bi\\), where \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are real numbers and \\(i^2 = \\text-1\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l12.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L12-ACTIVITY-033",
      "SourceSection": "12.3: Multiplication on the Complex Plane",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A number on the imaginary number line. It can be written as \\(bi\\), where \\(b\\) is a real number and \\(i^2 = \\text-1\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l12.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L12-ACTIVITY-034",
